{"id": "core-gradient-estimation-cfg-pp", "name": "Gradient Estimation CFG++", "family": "sampler", "subfamily": "multistep ODE, CFG++", "plain": "Same correction with slope taken from the unconditional prediction, and the base step using the CFG++ form. The cfg=1 shortcut is off. No \u03b1 factors, so on flow models it differs from euler_cfg_pp.", "math": "Symbols: x current latent; \u03c3=sigmas[i]; \u03c3'=sigmas[i+1]; D=denoised (x0 prediction after CFG); U=uncond_denoised; d=(x\u2212D)/\u03c3. \nd_u=(x\u2212U)/\u03c3; x_e=D+\u03c3'd_u; from i\u22651: x'=x_e+(\u03b3\u22121)(d_u\u2212d_u,old)(\u03c3'\u2212\u03c3), \u03b3=2.", "props": {"order": "nominal 2 from step 2", "stages": "1 (2 network passes, cfg=1 shortcut off)", "stochastic": "deterministic", "multistep": true, "prediction_space": "\u03c3, eps from U", "final_sigma0": "Explicit: \u03c3'=0 returns D.", "flow_const": "No CONST branch. Base step is D+\u03c3'(x\u2212U)/\u03c3, whereas euler_cfg_pp on CONST is (1\u2212\u03c3')D+\u03c3'(x\u2212(1\u2212\u03c3)U)/\u03c3; the two differ by exactly \u03c3'(D\u2212U) (algebra from the two lines, not run)."}, "evidence": [{"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:1588", "symbol": "sample_gradient_estimation_cfg_pp"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:1558", "symbol": "disable_cfg1_optimization"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:1563", "symbol": "uncond_denoised"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:1575", "symbol": "denoised + d"}, {"where": "ComfyUI/comfy/k_diffusion/sampling.py:1581", "symbol": "d_bar"}], "providers": [{"pack": "core", "author": "Comfy Org and contributors", "licence": "GPL-3.0", "kind": "original", "nodes": ["KSampler", "KSamplerAdvanced", "KSamplerSelect"], "note": "", "verdict": "", "risks": [], "res4lyf": false}], "providers_n": 1, "in_core": true, "live": false, "needs_pack": false, "core_ref": {"sampler_name": "gradient_estimation_cfg_pp", "node": "KSamplerSelect"}, "family_fit": [], "cla